# `*` is not defined element-wise on [char], because `*` is not defined on char:
# the element-wise table (src/tychoc.c:1102) gives the char arm `+` and `-` only.
# The positive half of the same rule is tests/char_elem_ops.ty.
#
# `[char]` is never written here -- it cannot be (docs/spec/03-types.md:75) -- it
# is inferred from the element type of `char_at` (src/tychoc.c:4867).
fn main():
    s := "ABC"
    a := [char_at(s, 0), char_at(s, 1)]
    b := a * a
    println(str(b[0]))
